j","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-02T21:20:00Z","updated_at":"2026-07-02T21:20:00Z","body":"@blueskythlikesclouds I can reproduce this with https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/xr/mobile_vr_interface_demo and switching it to the Forward+ renderer, so this seems to be broken for all stereo rendering scenarios. That demo is a handy one to add to your arsenal because it allows you to test rendering changes for stereo rendering without needing hardware. There are difference in the way OpenXR works so it doesn't catch all issues, but definitely helps loads.\n\nI'll see if I can figure out what exactly is breaking, hopefully it's something simple.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4870566315/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4870809786","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120832#issuecomment-4870809786","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120832","id":4870809786,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABIlKoug","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-02T22:00:06Z","updated_at":"2026-07-02T22:00:06Z","body":"Ok, so in a nutshell the issue happens because when creating uniform sets, they are often checked against the first shader variant under the (incorrect) assumption the uniform set is always the same for every variant. It wasn't a problem because in most cases it is just whether single or multi layer textures are used and we weren't checking for that until recently, those few places it was a problem due to other set differences have already been fixed up.\n\nThe solution here is to ensure we check against the correct (base) shader variant, but it looks like there are many places where this applies. Following up with stakeholders on how to best proceed.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4870809786/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]